  "notes": [
    "Each normalized champion is joined by an explicit pinned asset name to Riot character_id, then cross-checked by exact English display name and cost; no alphabetical or ordinal identifier inference is used.",
    "Example aliases: TFT18_Pebbles maps to DA_18_Sentry; TFT18_Sentinel to DA_Sentinel18; TFT18_Nidalee to DA_Nidalee18_AP; TFT18_Lux_Base to DA_Lux18_Base. Per-unit matched aliases are retained in sourceRecords.",
    "Riot renumbered two champions in the 16.18 client (live 18.2): Ivern 405 -> 404 and Lux 413 -> 405 (hexadecimal; 1029 -> 1028 and 1043 -> 1029), and 16.19 (live 18.3) keeps them. The catalog pinned from 16.17 on 2026-09-07 exported both wrongly from 18.2 until it was refreshed on 2026-09-23. MetaTFT's code/codeValue, a PBE build, already carried the new IDs; it is still not used as a fallback.",
    "Version 02 codes contain ten three-digit hexadecimal champion identifiers followed by TFTSet18; unused entries are 000. Items, star levels, hex positions, Alpha assignment and selected Lux origin are not encoded.",
    "Elder Dragon occupies one champion entry in the code even though he uses two board team slots."
  ],
